insonic maintained WebView lifetime and native-key patch

Upstream: github.com/wailsapp/go-webview2 v1.0.22
https://github.com/wailsapp/go-webview2/tree/v1.0.22

Original upstream files and MIT license are retained. The insonic additions
use Apache-2.0 (LICENSE.insonic). A native parent-window lifetime subclass
closes the WebView controller once on its owning UI thread during destruction.
The ordinary window procedure continues normally.

The insonic source tree contains third_party/go-webview2.source.json with
exact upstream and maintained source checksums. The main product source
revision binds this repository-local replacement; Go binary metadata records
the relative replacement path rather than an upstream checksum for the patch.

The maintained cleanup also balances owned COM interface references and the original UI-thread apartment initialization. The manifest lists both modified upstream files and every added file.

The native system-key extension copies original accelerator context on the
owned window UI thread. Claimed keys retain one handled disposition; the host
posts native menu work instead of directly entering modal UI in the callback. Other
accelerators retain their existing callback route.

While an owned native menu is active, the parent retains keyboard focus and
does not forward WM_SETFOCUS back into the browser. Menu exit restores the
previous owned child only while the same parent still owns foreground input.

Explicit disposable qualification can retain fixed navigation/resource callback
counts and the browser version for bounded failure evidence. It does not retain
request URLs, script contents or application data, or add browser calls.
